Console output of the L40S runs, captured 2026-09-25 on a single NVIDIA L40S of
a university Slurm cluster. Shell prompt lines removed; everything else is
verbatim program output, elided only where marked [...].

  python -m chia_loop.loop --bypass chia_loop/configs/bypass_synthesis_only.yaml \
      --peak-bw 864e9 --peak-flops 362e12

Environment: torch 2.9.1+cu128, Triton 3.5.1, Python 3.10.12,
NVIDIA L40S (compute capability 8.9, 46068 MiB), B=2 H=32 S=2048 D=128, bf16.

Two runs are recorded here: the first, before the sigmoid reference bug
described in RESULTS_L40S.md was found, and the final one after all three bugs
were fixed. Run 1 is kept because its eager baselines agree with the final
run's to within 0.5%, which is what establishes their reproducibility, and
because the failure is part of the result. Two intermediate runs, made while
the reference briefly carried an extra fp32 masking pass, are described in
RESULTS_L40S.md and are not reproduced here.


